@AC 2468[2]. Such persons are described in the Word... when their good is not as yet so much defiled; then, when it is defiled; and afterwards, when it is altogether defiled. @--[3]. @--[6]. @--[10]. @4174.

@4050[end]. Under <Lymph>, see this reference.

@4462[2]. Under <Most Ancient Church>, see this reference.

@5390[end]. They had been endowed with a certain intellectual faculty, which they had abused to defile even the holy things of the Word and of doctrine.

@5954[9]. Under <Defile-Polluere>, see these references. @AE 195[3].

@7091. They would thus defile the Divine. @7290[end].

@7902[2]. If there is one falsity... the truths themselves remaining are thus defiled...

@10049. The lowest and natural things are more defiled with evils and falsities than interior ones...

@10208[2]. The sanctuaries... were defiled when the people sinned.

@HH 302[end]. The good which flows in he defiles with merit.

@561. Hence the Divine cannot flow in, because the instant it does so, it is immersed in thoughts about self, and is defiled.

@DLW 420[end]. All the defilement of man is effected through falsities opposed to the truths of wisdom.

@421. The love or will is defiled in the understanding, and by it, if they are not elevated together. General article.

@424. Love denied in the understanding, and by it, becomes natural, sensuous, and corporeal. General article.

@AR 166. Under <Defile-Inquinare>, see these references. @620. @DLW 419.

@729. The Roman Catholic religiosity... has defiled and profaned the things of the Word and of the Church. Signified.

Defile.; Inquinare.
Defilement.; Inquinamentum.

@AC 6388. They thus not only defile genuine love or charity, but also pervert it.

@7090[3]. These things are darkness and defilements...

@HH 515. Nor have they denied their spiritual life by the grossnesses from honours and riches.

@DLW 419[2]. Through the understanding, the love... sees what the evils are which pollute and defile -conspurcant- the love.

@AR 166. "Who have not defiled their garments" (Revelation 3:4) = who are in truths, and have not defiled -conspurcaverunt- their worship through evils of life and the falsities thence.

@620. "These are they who have not been defiled with women" (Revelation 14:4) = that they have not adulterated the truths of the Church, and defiled -conspurcaverunt- them with falsities of faith.

@TCR 366[2]. The evil obstruct this influx by... spiritual defilements...

@AE 195. Under <Sardis>, see this reference.

@862. "These are they who have not been defiled with women" = those who have not falsified the truths of the Word.

