Defilement.; Pollutio.

@AC 4439. "Jacob heard that he had defiled Dinah his daughter" (Genesis 34:5) = conjunction not lawful... The defilement of marriages = conjunction not lawful.

@4460. "Because he defiled Dinah their sister" = initiation to conjunction.

@4503[9]. To "defile the houses, and fill the courts with the slain" (Ezekiel 9:7) = to profane goods and truths.

@4504. "Because they had defiled their sister" = because they had defiled -foedaverunt- the truth of faith.

@5954[9]. "Defiled garments" (Zechariah 3:3) = truths defiled -conspurcatis- by the falsities which are from evil. @AE 740[16].

@AE 195[3]. Thus are Knowledges from the Word polluted and defiled -conspurcantur- by the loves of self and of the world...

@388[15]. To "defile the temple of holiness" (Psalms 79:1) = to profane worship.

