@3589. Desirable and delectable things for the Divine Rational. Signified.

@--. "Dainties" = the delights which are of good and the pleasantnesses which are of truth; the delights which are of good are desirable things, and the pleasantnesses which are of truth are delectable ones; for the affection of good is what desires, and then the affection of truth is what delectates.

@3928. When he desires the things of Heaven...

@3944. The longing for interior truth. Signified.

@3945. The affection and longing for the things which are of marriage love. Signified.

@3946. That there is conjugial longing. Signified.

@3950. Longing on the part of the affection of external truth... that it may be conjoined. Signified.

