@--[end]. Temptation attacks that which man loves and desires.

@8564. The ardent longing for truth. Signified.

@8568. Increase of the longing for truth. Signified.

@--. To "thirst" = to have an appetite for and to desire, namely, truth.

@--. The desire of knowing truth is here described by to "thirst;" the desire for truth is signified by "I will not send thirst for waters, but for hearing the words of Jehovah."

@8847. From an intense longing he importuned to be admitted into Heaven.

@--[2]. As it were a blazing longing to put itself off...

@--[end]. By this was represented the nature of the longings of those who are in province to which the seminal vesicles correspond.

